Dear [redacted], 

This is to acknowledge receipt of your Access to Information Act (Act) request received on April 13, 2026, for:

Records (briefing notes, memos, legal opinions, risk assessments, posting orders, assignment instructions, selection criteria documents, and email correspondence) held by RCN, CJOC, JAG, and VCDS related to the selection, posting,
 and assignment of Royal Canadian Navy personnel embedded aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho (Republic of Korea Navy, KSS-III class submarine) during its trans-Pacific voyage from January 1 2024 – April 11, 2026, including:

1) Records describing the selection process, criteria, eligibility requirements, and authority for assigning RCN personnel to embedded positions aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho (Republic of Korea Navy, KSS-III class submarine)

2) Records related to the deployment of CAF members aboard a Republic of Korea Navy vessel, including consideration of applicable Korean military law (including Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea’s Military Criminal Act)

3) Records concerning the legal, human rights, or personnel policy implications of placing CAF members aboard a vessel governed by Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea's Military Criminal Act, which criminalizes consensual
 same-sex conduct between military personnel

4) Records concerning the embedded posting, including the timeline and authority for the assignment decision.

5) Records indicating whether candidates sexual orientation, gender, or gender identity were considered in selecting embedded positions, including any guidance on Article 92-6 and whether selected personnel were informed of its legal context aboard the ROKS
 Dosan Ahn Chang-ho.

Please use these keywords only in the context of RCN personnel embedded aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho, and not as standalone search terms: "Dosan Ahn Chang-ho"; "KSS-III"; "embedded"; "exchange personnel"; "posting criteria";
 "selection criteria"; "Article 92-6"; "Korean Military Criminal Act"; "sexual orientation"; "LGBTQ"; "homosexual"; "duty of care"; "personnel exchange Korea"; "joint exercises Korea"; "trans-Pacific"; "Esquimalt

Please note that every effort is being made to process your request within the prescribed 30-day time limit pursuant to the Act. In addition, your request will be processed in accordance with the Principles for Assisting Requesters as per the Treasury Board
 Secretariat's policies and guidance which can be found at: 
https://www.canada.ca/en/treasury-board-secretariat/services/access-information-privacy/access-information/supporting-tool-access-information-personal-information-requests-principles-assisting-requesters.html.

Please be advised that the response to your request will be sent to you through Connect (https://www.canadapost-postescanada.ca/cpc/en/business/postal-services/digital-mail/connect.page).
 A portable document format (PDF) of the records will be uploaded to and will remain available for viewing in the Connect portal for 60 days.

For any questions concerning your request or if you wish to opt-out of Connect and obtain a copy of your records via regular mail, please contact our office by email at atip-aiprp@forces.gc.ca.

